      "message": "I\u0027m confused how this works. If we are sitting here with key scanning disabled, and then scanning suddenly gets enabled, it seems the following will happen:\n- this task will wake\n- we will call keyboard_raw_drive_column(KEYBOARD_COLUMN_ALL)\n- we will check if a key is pressed\n\nBut if no key is pressed we will end up back here in task_wait_event(-1), only we\u0027ve never enabled the keyboard interrupt (keyboard_raw_enable_interrupt(1)). So, how does this wake up then when the user presses a key?\n\nI\u0027m not familiar enough with the key scanning task to know if it\u0027s indirectly enabled somewhere and it seems from comments like there are subtle race conditions enabling that interrupt.",
